{
 "queue": "security",
 "summary": "URGENT data-theft risk: Priya Raman (E004, Sales Director) reports that Hannah Wright (E018, Sales Development Rep, Sales, Chicago; manager Diego Alvarez E017) was seen by Diego exporting the full customer list to her personal Gmail last night. Current access: email, chat, hr_portal, crm. She is being terminated today and they want her locked out right away. Please assess and act right away. HR has been escalated separately to handle the termination."
}

{
 "queue": "hr",
 "summary": "Involuntary termination: Priya Raman (E004, Sales Director) reports that Hannah Wright (E018, Sales Development Rep, manager Diego Alvarez E017) is being terminated today after allegedly exporting the customer list to her personal Gmail. Per POL-OFF-02, HR handles this and coordinates when access is removed. Security has been escalated for the data-theft risk at the same time."
}

{
 "kind": "escalated",
 "message": "Thanks for raising this quickly, Priya. Under our policy for involuntary exits (POL-OFF-02), the helpdesk can't start offboarding or remove access for a termination itself, even when a manager asks. HR handles terminations and decides when access comes off. Because there's a risk of data theft, the policy also says Security must be told straight away.\n\nHere's what I've done:\n- **Security (ticket ESC-1001), marked urgent:** I passed on Diego's report that the customer list was exported to a personal Gmail account. I also listed Hannah Wright's (E018) current access: email, chat, HR portal and CRM. Security will look into it and decide how fast to lock her accounts.\n- **HR (ticket ESC-1002):** I asked them to handle the termination and when her access is removed.\n\nPlease expect Security and HR to contact you and Diego. Keep any evidence you have, such as what Diego saw and when, so you can give it to Security.",
 "cited_policy_ids": [
  "POL-OFF-02"
 ]
}
